    "title": "Fresno's airport mascot has officially come to life - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Miranda Adams ,\n2 hours ago\nFRESNO, Calif. ( KSEE/KGPE ) – Fresno Yosemite International Airport’s mascot has officially come to life.\nThe airport says Gordo, their giant blue-and-yellow bird in hiking boots, will be making appearances this month.\nGordo’s is a cross between California’s Yellow Warbler and Scrub Blue Jay , and the Spanish translation of his name, “fat,” is cleverly also the IATA location code for Fresno’s airport: “FAT.”\nHe was first introduced to the public in Aug. 2019 and designed by local muralist and designer Rudy Contreras, who previously worked at Disney.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to CBS47 and KSEE24 | News from YourCentralValley.com.",
